    "title": "Walters drives in game winner in Frontier League All-Star Game - NewsBreak",
    "text": "TROY, NY ( NEWS10 ) — The Tri-City ValleyCats hosted the 2025 Frontier League All-Star Game in front of a packed house at Joe Bruno Stadium on Wednesday night. ValleyCats third baseman, Ian Walters, drove in the winning run on an RBI single in the seventh inning to give the Atlantic Conference the 5-4 win. The ValleyCats were represented by 4 players on the roster, alongside Walters were Oscar Campos, Easton Klein and Delmar native, Arlo Marynczak. Klein was the only player other than Walters to appear in the game, pitching the second inning, allowing 3 runs (only 2 earned) while striking out a pair. The Capital region was represented in the home run derby as well which took place pre-game. Colonie grad, Tommy Kretzler, took part in the contest. Kretzler, who plays for the Brockton Rox, reached the semifinals after placing in the top 4 in the opening round. The ValleyCats return to regular season play on Friday when they open up a 3-game set with Trois-Rivieres at the Joe at 6:30 p.m. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.",
